Z||000001||theogre||07-16-2000||12:28 AM||||What's the problem again? Search for threads starting HOW TO: I did one on the DIS brick.<P>there's not much to it. If you take the brick off the block then make sure you teflon tape seal the threads of the bolts when you put them back. Also check/replace the O ring on the crank sensor. It gets hard and leaks if you disturb it.<P>The PIM only goes together one way. Make sure you put Dielectric grease in the crank sensor hole if you take it apart. Also clean it and put dielectric or better yet heat sink compound between the PIM and the aluminum mounting tray.<P>The only other place to get data on the brick is from an ALLdata CD/DVD, The factory book, or maybe the Popular mechanics CD's that you can get at K/Wall marts. (Those are done by ALLdata for Pop Mech.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||07-23-2000||08:57 PM||||sorry to dredge up an old post. first day off in two weeks. finaly got a chance to try coil pac change. easy enough and seems to have worked. but i said that when i got the code for the idle speed control too. drove for about an hour through the city, meant to get on xway but ended up at home again. guess i'll be wary of it a few days and hope i've got it this time. also changed plugs, wires. idle speed control (because of scan code), air and fuel filters. this was all done prior to the coils and made no improvement, except for the speed control which for some reason seemed to improve it but it went back to acting up the next day. coincidence? maybe two problems that i though were one?<P>last, if i disconnect a sensor should my check engine light come on? during my trouble shooting ( which largely consists of scatching my head and being confused) i pulled my manifold differential pressure leads because the manual says the ecm gets timing info from it also. the engine didn't change idle speed or smoothness (or lack thereof) and the check engine light didn't come on. maybe i didn't have it off long enough or something? just wondering in case i have to start looking again.||||reg||1
